# Do Not Run Database Queries

Never execute database operations yourself. The user runs all database commands.

## Do not run

- SQL against any database (`psql`, `sqlite3`, `mysql`, raw `SELECT`/`INSERT`/`UPDATE`/`DELETE`)
- Migration commands (`alembic upgrade`, `alembic downgrade`, `alembic stamp`)
- Scripts or one-off code that connect to and query the database
- ORM sessions against a live database to inspect or mutate data

## Instead

- Write or edit migration files, models, and repository code
- Tell the user which command to run and why (e.g. `alembic upgrade head`)
- Use existing tests or mock data when verification is needed without a live DB

## Examples

```bash
# ❌ Do not run
psql -c "SELECT * FROM games"
alembic upgrade head
python -c "from app.db import SessionLocal; ..."

# ✅ Provide the command for the user
# Run: alembic upgrade head
```
